-moduledoc """
SHA3-512 (FIPS 202), producing `bytes/0` byte digests, either in one shot
or incrementally.

The streaming functions thread an opaque `t:state/0` through `init/0`,
`update/2`, and `final/1`; each call returns a new state and leaves its
argument unchanged. Updates over large inputs yield to other processes
between chunks.

Unlike SHA-2, SHA-3 is not vulnerable to length extension attacks. Use it
when SHA-3 is required for interoperability; otherwise
`m:libsodium_crypto_generichash` is faster.

```erlang
Digest = libsodium_crypto_hash_sha3512:crypto_hash_sha3512(<<"hello world">>),
64 = byte_size(Digest),
